  {
    "id": "class-04-conjugation-001",
    "appliesTo": "verb-ichidan",
    "form": "ta",
    "explanation": [
      {
        "en": "The casual past affirmative (\"ta-form\") is derived from the te-form by changing the final え sound to あ: 食べて→食べた, 見て→見た, 寝て→寝た. Ichidan verbs simply swap て→た."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "form": "ta",
        "surface": "食べた",
        "reading": "たべた"
      },
      {
        "form": "ta",
        "surface": "見た",
        "reading": "みた"
      },
      {
        "form": "ta",
        "surface": "寝た",
        "reading": "ねた"
      }
    ],
    "lessonIds": [
      "class-04"
    ],
    "origin": "course",
    "source": [
      {
        "file": "Class N°04 - synthesis & assignments.pdf",
        "page": 14
      }
    ]
